# Thoughts After Bootcamp Level 2

Before this session I thought fully autonomous prediction markets were still a bit theoretical.  

After reading the code I realise Ritual already gives us the primitive we need:
- Reliable on-chain scheduling
- Secure off-chain data access
- Lightweight on-chain parsing

The decision to treat oracle failures as Invalid instead of forcing a YES/NO is pure product wisdom.  
It prioritises fairness over “always having a result”.

Also love that each retry can pick a different executor — small detail, big reliability gain.

This is the kind of workshop that makes me want to build more things on the network.  
Looking forward to mainnet and to seeing what the community creates next.
